WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.373
- [Man] This space.

00:00:01.373 --> 00:00:04.360
(light electronica music)

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.840
How could we possibly make this space

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.330
the perfect office and studio?

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:12.170
Well, it requires a lot
of trips to Home Depot.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:14.080
Where I first bought
these big yellow tools,

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.020
that presumably were exactly what I needed

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:17.685
to start doing this.

00:00:17.685 --> 00:00:21.390
(light electronica music)

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.890
Quickly, the space devolved into chaos.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.010
It hit rock bottom

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:28.240
on the day when there was
just a giant pile of cabinets

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.380
appliances, drywall, and
heaven knows what else,

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.600
all stacked right here in the
middle of this front room.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.740
It's moments like these

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:39.260
when you wonder if this is
all ever gonna come together,

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.990
but then the building starts.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:43.220
More Home Depot and shipments.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.400
So many shipments,

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.470
so many boxes.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.380
There's hard wood floor.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.370
There's weird electrical
problems that come up

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:50.940
and suddenly you're
paying your electrician

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.240
way more than you hoped
you'd be paying him.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.073
- I see.

00:00:54.073 --> 00:00:56.720
- But slowly it starts to come together.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:57.553
It starts to look

00:00:57.553 --> 00:00:59.940
like the kind of space
that you want to be in,

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.770
work in, create in,

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:04.070
but there's still a long way to go.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:06.270
Next comes the visit to a rug warehouse

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:08.770
where a man who came from
Afghanistan 30 years ago

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:10.490
shows you a million rugs

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:13.250
and you decide how
you'll cover your floors.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:14.750
And will these rugs actually dampen

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.330
the acoustics of the room,
so we can get good audio.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:18.620
I sure hope so.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:19.453
Before you know it,

00:01:19.453 --> 00:01:21.610
the owner has forcibly
invited you to his restaurant

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:23.090
that's just right next door.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:25.510
Where he gives you piles of steaming kebab

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:27.960
and rice and chickpeas and tea

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.660
and beautifully fresh bread.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.080
Henry, do you love this food?

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:31.913
Back to work.

00:01:31.913 --> 00:01:33.620
Your child is now sitting on the floor.

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.310
Wait, is that asbestos tile?

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:36.143
It probably is.

00:01:36.143 --> 00:01:37.520
I should probably get him out of here.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.260
Scan the internet for the right tile,

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:40.270
back to Home Depot.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.250
The boys are in their
PJ's because it's bedtime.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:44.643
But for some reason we
have to go to Home Depot.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:48.320
I don't really remember what happens next.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.870
I just know that after a
million trips to Home Depot

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:53.120
and a million passes on this place,

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:56.830
a million tiny details, it's done.

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:58.090
This is what the place looked like

00:01:58.090 --> 00:01:59.980
when we bought it in December.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:02.219
And now, it looks like this.

00:02:02.219 --> 00:02:06.136
(heavy bass electronica music)

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:14.700
We wanted a space that didn't feel

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.950
too much like a proper studio,

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.850
but rather a place you would
live in, spend time in.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:21.260
And while I had some of the vision

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.850
for how it would be remodeled

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:24.850
and what kind of
countertops it would have.

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:27.440
Iz was the one with the
interior design vision.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:28.990
She put a giant effort

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:31.780
into collecting a set
of textures and designs

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:34.060
that felt that once natural to us,

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.910
but also interesting and like a statement.

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:38.760
The space has all sorts of textures

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.160
that means something to us,

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.290
like this Pendleton blanket

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:43.220
that comes from our home state of Oregon

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:44.053
or this pillow

00:02:44.053 --> 00:02:46.160
that we picked up in a
market in Wahaca, Mexico

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.510
when we were there in December.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:49.330
This beautiful tan couch was sent to us

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.440
by Article, an online couch company

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.560
that has also sent us these
stools and this table.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.130
All of this providing a unified texture

00:02:57.130 --> 00:03:00.630
that feels so natural to
the space, it feels artful

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:02.060
and yet comfortable.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.990
And all these textures a top,

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:07.113
these Afghan rugs that we
got from that warehouse.

00:03:08.345 --> 00:03:11.721
(heavy electronica music)

00:03:11.721 --> 00:03:13.680
All the gear people who are like,

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.090
hey, we came here to learn
about your gear storage

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:18.670
and your studio workflow.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:19.570
I will get to that.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:22.900
I promise, but just take
a minute to just revel

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:24.603
in the beauty of this room.

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.530
Okay, so for all the gear people out there

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:28.780
here's something you're gonna like.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.900
See these bars up here on the ceiling.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.530
This is a track

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:33.760
with a hanging arm

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:35.670
that allows us to mount
whatever we need to,

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:38.300
microphones, light, a top-down camera.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.870
It can all be mounted right here

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:42.010
with the flexibility
to slide back and forth

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.350
along this front room.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:46.600
This front room is kind of
our primary shooting space.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.620
We can shoot here the couch

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.060
or if we need to get
more of a studio look,

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.870
we can pull down the seamless's,

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.950
which give us a variety of
different colors to work with.

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:56.600
Moving over to the kitchen,

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.770
this is where you see my pride and joy.

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:01.350
This giant slab of Walnut butcher block.

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:03.210
I worked really hard to get this sucker.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.310
It came from a woodworking
shop in Illinois.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:07.440
And when it got here, it was
just a raw piece of wood.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.250
And I spent a lot of hours

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:11.860
beveling it and sanding it and oiling it.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:12.710
And it's safe to say

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:15.710
that I now have a very special
bond with this piece of wood.

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.460
The kitchen serves a similar purpose.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:18.680
It allows us to film here,

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:21.290
but it's a totally functional
kitchen with snacks.

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.865
And most importantly, a nice coffee setup.

00:04:23.865 --> 00:04:27.350
(funky electronica music)

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:30.900
We use this new setup from
Fellow, it's the stag system.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.763
And I really liked it so far.

00:04:32.763 --> 00:04:35.420
(funky electronica music)

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:38.350
Irving Farms, a roastery
and cafe in New York City

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:41.070
sent us this beautiful
coffee and we love it.

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:42.150
It tastes different

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.680
than any other bags we've
ever had in the house.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.010
And I'm just really glad it exists.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.640
Okay, so beside the kitchen
we have this audio table,

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.550
where we have two mics
that are always setup,

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:55.080
they're USB mics, and we can
record voiceovers or podcasts.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.860
It's also a place where
presumably we could have a meal.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.100
And if we ever have guests

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.690
who want to work out of the space,

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:02.143
this would be their place.

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.050
Okay, so now into the office area,

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:08.260
but first you probably noticed
all these framed photos

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:09.650
that we have around the space.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:12.560
These were given to us by a
company called Frame Bridge.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:14.720
And I have to say, this has
been one of my favorite parts

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.040
of this whole experience.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:16.992
We take a lot of pictures

00:05:16.992 --> 00:05:20.650
and usually only see them on
computer or phone screens.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:24.280
So to see them in these giant
frames all around the space,

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.790
it's been incredibly gratifying.

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:29.623
It's like art with a memory baked into it.

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:33.262
Okay, now onto the office.

00:05:33.262 --> 00:05:36.010
Remember now it used to look like this

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:38.740
with new paint and floors
and bunch of decor.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:40.605
It now looks like this.

00:05:40.605 --> 00:05:44.188
(funky electronica music)

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.360
The anchor to a good workspace

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:55.550
is a good desk and chair setup.

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:58.600
And for this, we are so, so, so grateful

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:00.580
that we found a company called Fully.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.192
Fully is based out of our
home, Portland Oregon.

00:06:03.192 --> 00:06:07.520
And we just have fallen
in love with these desks.

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:10.860
They make these sit stand
desks that are totally solid.

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:14.680
We have the bamboo Jarvis
desk with this subtle cutout.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.140
And I have to say, I'm in love.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:17.500
They have loads of accessories

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.658
like this laptop and monitor arm,

00:06:19.658 --> 00:06:22.797
or this magnetic hook,
these file cabinets.

00:06:22.797 --> 00:06:24.400
Along with the desks,

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.980
they send us these chairs
and they look kind of funky.

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:28.500
But the whole point of these chairs is

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:30.510
that they get you moving
throughout the day.

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:32.560
You can sit in a bunch
of different positions

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.900
which I've found to be really
good for my very fidgety self.

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:38.750
These desks and chairs
have changed my world.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:41.320
They've made my work day a
totally different experience.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:43.630
So by the way, I'm gonna
plan to make a video entirely

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:44.810
about my working setup

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:46.790
and hacks that I use for
a more efficient day.

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:49.600
But let's move on to
the rest of the space.

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:53.037
Iz intentionally gave me
this entire wall to myself

00:06:53.037 --> 00:06:55.570
and I'm very, very happy about it.

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:56.650
And to populate it,

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:59.920
of course, I chose my favorite
thing in the world maps.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.780
I found this old map on eBay that was

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:04.970
in like an elementary
school and it's been lovely.

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:07.110
I find myself just staring
at it during the day.

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.720
You'll also see more of
these Frame Bridge frames

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:11.710
and some miscellaneous photos

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:13.930
from Switzerland and other travels.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:16.780
I'm gonna keep adding to this
gallery and changing it up.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:20.460
Okay, let's talk about gear, finally gear.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:22.600
Everyone's here to talk
about gear I'm sure.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:24.220
I love pegboards.

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:25.690
I got these cheap pegboards

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:27.840
at Home Depot and spray
painted them black.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.840
And this allowed us to take
all of the gear and accessories

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:33.050
and camera stuff out from under our bed

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.300
and our children's closet

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:37.200
and in every crevice of
our house and put it here.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:40.210
It took a long time to
develop a coherent system

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:42.870
to get everything organized
and up on this wall.

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:45.180
But the payoff has been huge.

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:46.380
Over here, we have this closet

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:49.210
with a charging station
that is firm and permanent.

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:51.081
It's the first time that I've ever had

00:07:51.081 --> 00:07:53.370
any sort of solid,
permanent charging station.

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:55.500
And it's been a dream come true.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.306
SD cards, tripods,

00:07:57.306 --> 00:07:59.870
they all have a place
and they're not competing

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:03.263
with four people living in
700 square feet any longer.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.120
Iz of course has her desk and her wall,

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:11.070
which is full of gorgeous
plants and knick-knacks.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:13.529
Many of them coming from our travels.

00:08:13.529 --> 00:08:16.260
(light electronica music)

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.900
So that's our studio.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:20.860
It's been a big investment
of time and money for us.

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:21.890
But after years

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:25.330
of recording voiceovers
under blankets in my bedroom

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:28.030
and stuffing camera gear
into our children's closets,

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:31.460
we're finally investing in a
space that spurs creativity

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:33.550
and gives us room to make more stuff

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:36.090
with the least amount
of friction possible.

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:37.820
We're excited about this place

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:39.910
and what it means for our future.

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:42.974
And you'll be seeing it
a lot more in our videos.

00:08:42.974 --> 00:08:45.890
(bells ringing music)

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:47.750
I just wanna clarify one
thing really quickly.

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:50.920
In this video, I talk a lot
about the products that we use.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:53.130
Some of this stuff was
sent to us for free.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.949
I want to be clear that

00:08:54.949 --> 00:08:57.320
all of these items are
things that we actually use.

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:59.400
And none of the brands that sent us stuff

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.120
paid us or told us what to say.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.400
They had no control editorially

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:06.010
over what we said about their product.

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:08.000
For the stuff that I bought personally,

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.810
I will leave an Amazon link for.

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:13.060
I made sure that all of the
brands that sent us stuff,

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:16.300
we get no kickbacks if you
decide to go buy a Fully desk

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.560
or an Article couch or
something from Frame Bridge.

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:20.320
I wanted to make sure that
there was a separation

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:22.950
from their influence in
how we talked about them.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:25.189
Plus stuff that I bought
for myself on Amazon,

00:09:25.189 --> 00:09:28.610
that stuff does support Izzy's channel.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:31.100
She has an affiliates account with Amazon.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:31.933
It's important that I clarify this

00:09:31.933 --> 00:09:33.230
because I want you to know

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:36.230
that everything I talked
about here was 100% based

00:09:36.230 --> 00:09:40.740
on my own evaluation and critique
and usage of these items.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:42.070
So thanks for watching.

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:45.585
And let me know if you have
any questions about the space.

00:09:45.585 --> 00:09:49.085
(light electronica music)

